- !<Text/9aa8741a-a683-44df-9ddd-7c0dfdca3b12>
  PrefabRemaps:
    []
  Name: Text
  Enabled: true
  RenderOrder: 200
  StretchMode: Stretch
  VerticalAlignment: Center
  HorizontalAlignment: Left
  MeshShadowMode: None
  ShadowColor: {x: 1.000000, y: 1.000000, z: 1.000000, w: 1.000000}
  ShadowDensity: 1.000000
  Text: |
    READ AND DISABLE!  
    Mocopi Receiver allows you to hook up the Sony Mocopi Sensor to Lens Studio and Spectacles using WebSockets!  Please check the Package README.md for a quickstart guide in details.   Step 1
    
    Setup Mocopi and the Mocopi app 
    
    Step 2
    
    Find your IP Address and add it to the Mocopi App > Settings > External Connections and add it to the input field in the Websocket Client Script
    
    Step 3
    
    Start the local server in the LocalServerExampleFolder on your machine.
    
    If using local server, make sure your connection is public and not protected. If using local server, you won't need to deploy the hosted server. 
    
    If using forwarded server, make sure that you deploy the hosted server. This will be allowing a more solid solution for Spectacles, but you will still need to spin the forwarded local server that send the animation frame to railway > that spectacles gets. 
    
    Step 4
    
    See the avatar synchronizing in Lens Studio?
    You are ready to build on Spectacles. 

  Editable: false
  ShowEditingPreview: true
  TouchHandler: !<reference> 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  SizeToFit: false
  FontSize: 55
